# Toronto Rising — seat occupancy terms (mandatory)

Two states are easy to conflate. Keep a **bright line** between them in code, comments, docs, Linear, and chat.

| Term | Meaning | Field / authority |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Occupied seat** | A PC or NPC holds a numbered chair (`tableSlot`). | `sessionScene.seatSlots[seat].tableSlot` |
| **Present** | Occupied and narratively in the scene — lit, fully visible. | `isPresent` (scene library + control-board token flip) |
| **Absent / Not Present** | Occupied but narratively out of the scene — seat dark, chair/sheet/hand stay. Also: a seated NPC standing on the stage. | `isPresent == false` |
| **Disconnected / Not Connected** | A PC whose client is not connected. Mid-session it only darkens the seat; at the next blindfold checkpoint it becomes `absentFromSession`. | `PC.isSeatConnected(color)` (`core/player_connection.ttslua`) |
| **Unoccupied seat** | No chair: an NPC removed from the table, or a PC with `absentFromSession`. Pile stashed once; table transitions never move it. | NPC `slotEmpty`; PC `absentFromSession` |

## The bright line

- **"Absent", "not present", "out of the scene"** (alone) always mean the **narrative** state of a **connected** player. Flexible wording is fine here.
- **`absentFromSession`** may only be described with **connection** language: "disconnected", "not connected". Never call it plain "Absent".
- **Connection is the only authority** for `absentFromSession`. No scene, table, phase, control-board, or panel action may set or clear it. A connect clears it **immediately** (seat restored); a disconnect only darkens the seat until the next blindfold checkpoint sets it.

## Push back on ambiguous wording

When the author (or another agent's note) uses "absent", "remove", "unseat", "not at the table", or similar in a way that could mean **either** narrative absence **or** a disconnected PC, **stop and ask** which one is meant before writing code or docs. Quote the ambiguous phrase and offer the two readings in plain English. Do not guess.

Canonical model, checkpoint list, and debug mode: [`docs/solutions/seat-occupancy-and-connection.md`](../../docs/solutions/seat-occupancy-and-connection.md).
